  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Delaware has received $155M in federal contract obligations so far in FY2026 to date. Federal buying in Delaware includes 2,756 awards with an average award size of $56.2K, and obligations fell 57.9% year over year. Annual obligations have moved from $321M in FY21 to $155M in FY26, with intermediate totals of $81.3M in FY22, $325M in FY23, $337M in FY24, and $368M in FY25. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer in FY2026 to date, obligating $68M, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $31M and the Department of Health and Human Services with $16.9M. Stonewin International, LLC is the top vendor in FY2026 to date with $13.1M, followed by AQUIA NAVA II LLC with $11.8M and CORBALT, LLC with $10.8M. Other notable industry categories in FY2026 to date include Other Computer Related Services at $17.8M, Petroleum Refineries at $13.1M, and Custom Computer Programming Services at $10.9M. These figures reflect fiscal year to date totals and are partial for the current year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has federal contracting in Delaware changed year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 57.9% year over year. Fiscal-year totals show a multi-year pattern: FY21 $321M, FY22 $81.3M, FY23 $325M, FY24 $337M, FY25 $368M, FY26 $155M. The current-year total of $155M is a partial, fiscal year to date figure. Buyers and award counts accompany that total: 2,756 awards at an average award size of $56.2K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate Delaware contracting?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $68M in FY2026 to date, the largest agency buyer. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $31M and the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $16.9M in the same period. STONEWIN INTERNATIONAL, LLC received $13.1M and AQUIA NAVA II LLC received $11.8M in FY2026 to date, followed by CORBALT, LLC at $10.8M."
      }
    ]
